  "body": "What happens: a model does not remember the file that it came from. `ImportModel` keeps the name, the mesh and the import settings only (`crates/app/src/commands/import_model.rs`). When the source file changes, the user must import it again by hand.\n\nExpected:\n- An imported model keeps its source path and the SHA-256 of the file that it read. The `.camproj` file saves the two values. A project that has no values still opens.\n- While the project is open, CamCraft checks the source file of each model. When the file has a new hash, CamCraft imports it again through `CommandKind::ImportFile`, under the same model name. The existing update path marks the operations Stale.\n- CamCraft never regenerates a toolpath or posts G-code because of this. The user does that.\n- A source file that is missing or that CamCraft cannot read does not change the model. The status line says so by name, one time.\n- The user can turn off the update for a model (\"Unlink\").\n- An MCP tool reads and sets the link.\n\nWhy: Solidcraft proposes \"Send to CamCraft\" (Solidcraft RFC 0001, phases 1 and 3: https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcraft/blob/main/docs/rfcs/0001-craft-bridge.md). Each save in Solidcraft writes the `.sc` file again. With this issue, CamCraft updates the part after each save.\n\nDepends on: the issue for opening a model file from the command line (#2462).\n\nDone means: a test changes a source file and finds the model updated and its operations Stale; a test finds an unchanged model when the file is missing; a `.camproj` round trip keeps the link; an older `.camproj` opens.\n\nSuggested labels (I cannot set labels): `enhancement`, `P6`, `effort:high`, `area:ui`, `source:agent`.\n",
